      "assessment": {
        "nobel_worthiness": "Optical lattice clocks have transformed precision timekeeping and created broadly enabling tests and measurement capabilities.",
        "attribution": "Katori introduced the magic-wavelength lattice-clock concept and Ye made decisive experimental advances toward leading-performance clocks.",
        "maturity": "The technique has been independently reproduced, steadily improved, and used as a durable precision-measurement platform.",
        "uncertainties": [
